{
  "slug": "terse-md",
  "name": "Terse Md",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Compresses Claude instruction files (CLAUDE.md, memory files, SKILL.md) into dense closed-schema YAML — typically 50–70% fewer tokens. Verified lossless by meaning via a mandatory round-trip review: source prose is normalized, compressed to YAML, decompressed back to prose, and shown side-by-side so you can approve that no rule was dropped or invented. Closed-vocabulary schema (rules, transforms, triggers, thresholds, meta) makes the output deterministic and hand-editable. Runs entirely inside Claude Code; no API key, no external service, no network calls.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **3 commands**.\n\n- **Commands** (3): `analyze` (Scan instruction files under a path, count tokens, sample-compress the largest file, report estimated savings), `run` (Compress a Markdown instruction file to validated YAML with round-trip review), `test` (Idempotence check)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install terse-md@claude-community` from `marcelopaniza/terse-md`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "wrapper",
  "wrapper": "command",
